WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:04.920
If you've seen Logan in the movie theatre
you might have got to see the secret Deadpool

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.649
2 teaser which plays just before the main
movie.

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:11.280
It's a fun little short that gives us some
nice easter eggs for the Merc With The Mouth's

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.550
upcoming sequel.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.789
The scene isn't part of the main Logan movie,
so I won't be discussing Logan spoilers in

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.390
this video, but obviously there are spoilers
for the Deadpool teaser and speculation about

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.390
Deadpool 2.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.230
If you prefer, you can check out my spoiler-free
review of Logan here and come back and watch

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.680
this video after you've seen the teaser.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.890
The scene begins with Ryan Reynolds as Wade
Wilson walking past an alley where an old

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.800
man is being held up at gunpoint.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.530
He pulls down his hoodie, shakes his head
and says "not on my watch, motherfucker" and

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.250
runs to a phone booth opposite a movie theatre
which just happens to be playing Logan.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:47.079
After he gets into the phone booth, John Williams'
Superman theme starts up and he begins to

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:50.330
change out of his regular clothes into his
Deadpool costume.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:54.460
Cries and pleas for help come from the man
being mugged as Wade struggles hilariously

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.859
to get into his suit.

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:59.820
All the while the epic Superman theme is playing
and there's a cheekily amusing moment where

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.760
Ryan Reynolds presses his bare butt up against
the phone booth glass.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.710
Just as Wade's almost finished, there's a
loud gunshot followed by silence.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.460
Deadpool finishes getting dressed as quick
as he can, exits the booth and runs slo-mo

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.200
across the street to the rising Superman anthem.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.040
When he reaches the guy who's been shot, the
theme cuts out and Deadpool jokes about spending

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.990
way too long in the phone booth.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:23.579
Deadpool then decides to lie down and rest
his head on the dead guy and starts eating

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:25.600
a tub of the man's ice cream.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.060
Deadpool is his usual meta-wisecracking self
in this teaser, making jokes about how weird

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.549
it is there's a phone booth on the street,
how he should have used his cell phone to

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:37.470
ring 911, and how other superheroes get changed
so quickly.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.700
He also pokes fun at Logan who he says probably
would have saved the dead guy as he doesn't

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.540
have to change into anything as his costume's
just a tank top and jeans.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:49.799
And as he eats the ice cream he says "ow,
brain freeze", a possible little nod to X-Men:

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:53.469
Apocalypse's deleted "brain freeze" scene
where Nightcrawler thinks he's frozen his

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:55.860
brain after drinking an iced drink.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:00.240
The words "Deadpool Coming Not Soon Enough"
then appear on screen followed by a scrolling

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.969
screen of text in which we get a Deadpool-style
commentary on Ernest Hemmingway's Pulitzer

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:08.950
prize-winning novel "The Old Man And The Sea",
complete with references to the Fresh Prince

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.210
and Marilyn Monroe.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:14.880
So, that was the scene; now, let's jump back
to some easter eggs snuck in around the phone

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.880
booth.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.670
First up is some graffiti which reads "Nathan
Summers Cumming Soon!"

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:19.860
scrawled on the phone booth.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:24.320
This is a big tease to Cable who we know is
in Deadpool 2 and perhaps a hint that we'll

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.360
have a casting announcement soon.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.400
Recent news claims that David Harbour who
played Chief Jim Hopper in Strangers Things

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.070
has screen-tested for the role alongside Ryan
Reynolds.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.650
Michael Shannon was apparently also in the
running but dropped out because of scheduling

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:37.650
issues.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.950
There's also speculation that Cable might
be played by Pierce Brosnan after Ryan Reynolds

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.480
shared a photo of himself with Brosnan and
Hugh Jackman earlier this year.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.670
For anyone who doesn't know, Cable is the
son of Cyclops and Jean Grey-clone Madelyne

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:55.380
Pryor, and he's a time-travelling mutant cyborg
with a cybernetic eye, bionic arms, superhuman

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.140
strength, and telepathic and telekinetic powers.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.700
In the comics, Cable also established the
X-Force, basically an off-shoot of the X-Men,

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.370
so he could be tied in with that movie too
once it gets off the ground.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.450
By the way, there's also some graffiti which
reads "REY" on the movie theatre behind the

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.010
phone booth, probably a little nod to Reynolds
himself.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:17.350
And when Deadpool emerges from the booth,
you can also spot some Firefly posters.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:22.200
Although Reynolds was in a 2008 movie called
"Fireflies in the Garden", it's more likely

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.610
a reference to Morena Baccarin who starred
in Firefly and played Vanessa in Deadpool.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.530
So, guys what do you think of the Deadpool
short?

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.980
And how hyped are you for Deadpool 2 and who
do you think should be cast as Cable?

